.\" microdlna.conf man page
.TH microdlna.conf 5 "October 2012"
.SH NAME
microdlna
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B microdlna
is a light weight but very functional DLNA server. In most cases, the defaults 
do not need modifications. A configuration file is only read when given with
\-f; the microdlna service uses /etc/microdlna.conf. Local users without system
root access can run microdlna with their own configuration file, or with no
file and \-\-option=value command line options instead.

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
The following are user configurable options in /etc/microdlna.conf.
microdlna runs as the user that starts it unless \fBuser\fP is set, so make sure
that user can read the media. An ordinary user that cannot write the default
log and pid locations gets per-user ones under $XDG_STATE_HOME (or
~/.local/state) and $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR.

.IP "\fBuser\fP"
User name or uid to switch to after starting. Empty (the default) keeps
running as the user that started microdlna.

.IP "\fBfriendly_name\fP"
The name you want your media server seen as, EG: friendly_name=Home Media Server

.IP "\fBport\fP"
.nf
Port for HTTP (descriptions, SOAP, media transfer) traffic etc. A port set here
or on the command line is used exactly; without one, the first free port from
8200 upwards is used. Instances not on 8200 get a UUID and default name that
include the port, so clients see them as separate servers.
.fi

.IP "\fBnetwork_interface\fP"
Network interfaces to serve, comma delimited. Maximum is 8 interfaces. Defaults to all.

.IP "\fBstrict_dlna\fP"
.nf
Set this to strictly adhere to DLNA standards. 
This will allow server-side downscaling of very large JPEG images,
which may hurt JPEG serving performance on (at least) Sony DLNA products.
.fi

.IP "\fBnotify_interval\fP" 
Notify interval in seconds. The default is 895 seconds.


.IP "\fBminissdpdsocket\fP"
.nf
Specify the path to the MiniSSDPd socket, 
EG: minissdpdsocket=/var/run/minissdpd.sock
.fi

.IP "\fBserial\fP"
.nf
Serial number the daemon will report to clients in its XML description. 
Defaults to 12345678
.fi

.IP "\fBmodel\fP"
.nf
Model number the daemon will report to clients in its XML description. 
Defaults to 1
.fi

.IP "\fBmedia_dir\fP" 
.nf
Path to the directory containing the media files microdlna should share. 
Use this option multile times if you have more than one directory to share. 

Example:
 media_dir=/opt/multimedia/videos
 media_dir=/opt/multimedia/movies
.fi
.PP
You can also restrict an entry to a specific media type, you do this
by using the following syntax: 
.nf
   the letter 'A', 'V' or 'P', followed by a comma (',') followed by the path.
   The meaning of the first letter is as follows:
                      'A' for audio files
                      'V' for video files
                      'P' for image files

    For example, if you want to include only video files located
    in /opt/multimedia/videos directory, and only music
    in /opt/multimedia/music, then you would use
                       media_dir=V,/opt/multimedia/videos
                       media_dir=A,/opt/multimedia/music

    Another example would be
                       media_dir=V,/opt/multimedia/videos
                       media_dir=V,/opt/multimedia/movies
                       media_dir=A,/opt/multimedia/music

    Or, if you did not care what type it finds, then you could use
                       media_dir=/opt/multimedia/videos
                       media_dir=/opt/multimedia/movies
                       media_dir=/opt/multimedia/music

    You can mix it up, find anything in music, but only Videos, in videos and movies
                       media_dir=V,/opt/multimedia/videos
                       media_dir=V,/opt/multimedia/movies
                       media_dir=/opt/multimedia/music

.fi

.IP "\fBpresentation_url\fP"
.nf
Default presentation url is http address on port 80
EG: presentation_url=http://www.mediaserver.lan/index.php
.fi

.IP "\fBdb_dir\fP"
Where microdlna stores the data files, including Album cache files. If it is
not set, no database is built: each folder is read from disk when a client
browses it. Durations, resolutions, tags and thumbnails are learned only for
small folders (see \fBprobe_limit\fP) and played files, and kept in memory.
Search, the Artist/Album/Genre views, bookmarks and TiVo support need a
database.

.IP "\fBvideo_extensions\fP, \fBaudio_extensions\fP, \fBimage_extensions\fP"
File extensions served as video, audio and pictures, matched case-insensitively
and separated by '/' or ','. Setting one replaces its whole list; an empty value
keeps the default:
.nf
 video: mpg/mpeg/avi/divx/xvid/asf/wmv/mp4/m4v/mts/m2ts/m2t/ts/vob/mkv/webm/flv/mov/3gp/rm/rmvb
 audio: mp3/flac/fla/flc/wma/asf/m4a/m4b/aac/mp4/m4p/wav/ogg/opus/mka/pcm/3gp/dsf/dff
 image: jpg/jpeg/png/webp
.fi
Extensions without a built-in tag reader are probed with libavformat. Pictures
other than JPEG are served as they are, without resized versions.

.IP "\fBsort_transliteration\fP"
Without \fBdb_dir\fP: how names are transliterated for sorting (folders first,
then a natural sort, so ep2 comes before ep10). \fBpinyin\fP (the default)
gives Chinese its context-aware pinyin from \fBpinyin_dict\fP and treats
everything else like \fBunidecode\fP; \fBicu\fP uses ICU's transliterator and
is several times slower; \fBunidecode\fP sorts like Python
natsorted(key=unidecode(t).lower()). Keys are cached, so each name is
transliterated once.

.IP "\fBpinyin_dict\fP"
The gzipped dictionary of \fBsort_transliteration=pinyin\fP, by default
/usr/share/microdlna/pinyin-dict.txt.gz.

.IP "\fBprobe_limit\fP"
Without \fBdb_dir\fP: a folder with at most this many media files (default 30)
has them probed while the client waits; larger folders are not. Played files
are always probed in the background. 0 disables probing while browsing.

.IP "\fBprobe_time\fP"
Without \fBdb_dir\fP: the longest a browse waits for probing, in milliseconds
(default 500). The rest is finished in the background and shows next time.
Waiting is limited to a tenth of the time overall, so a burst of browses (VLC
opens every subfolder of the folder it shows) never stalls the server.

.IP "\fBlog_dir\fP"
Path to the directory where the log file upnp-av.log should be stored, this 
defaults to /var/log

.IP "\fBlog_level\fP"
Set this to change the verbosity of the information that is logged each 
section can use a different level: off, fatal, error, warn, info, or debug
.nf

Example
log_level=general,artwork,database,inotify,scanner,metadata,http,ssdp,tivo=warn
.fi

.IP "\fBinotify\fP"
Set to 'yes' to enable inotify monitoring of the files under media_dir 
to automatically discover new files. Set to 'no' to disable inotify.
This is the default, and it has no effect when \fBdb_dir\fP is empty.

.IP "\fBalbum_art_names\fP"
This should be a list of file names to check for when searching for album art
and names should be delimited with a forward slash ("/").
.nf

Example
album_art_names=Cover.jpg/cover.jpg/AlbumArtSmall.jpg/albumartsmall.jpg/AlbumArt.jpg
/albumart.jpg/Album.jpg/album.jpg/Folder.jpg/folder.jpg/Thumb.jpg/thumb.jpg

.fi

.IP "\fBenable_tivo\fP"
Set this to yes to enable support for streaming .jpg and .mp3 files to a TiVo 
supporting HMO, default is no.

.IP "\fBtivo_discovery\fP"
Set this to 'beacon' to use the legacy TiVo broadcast discovery method. Defaults to
using Bonjour if Avahi support is available.

.IP "\fBroot_container\fP" 
Use a different container as the root of the tree exposed to clients.
.nf
The possible values are:
             '.' to use the standard container;
             'B' to use the "Browse Directory" container (this is the default);
             'M' to use the "Music" container;
             'V' to use the "Video" container;
             'P' to use the "Pictures" container.
  If you specify 'B' and the client device is audio only, then
  "Music/Folders" will be used as root container and you wont see Videos.
  Ignored when db_dir is empty: the root is then always the folder tree.
.fi

.IP "\fBforce_sort_criteria\fP"
Always force SortCriteria to this value, regardless of the SortCriteria passed by the client.
.nf
You may prepend the sort criteria with "!" to alter the titles of the objects so that they
will be alphanumerically sorted in the order you specify here, to work around clients that do
their own alphanumeric sorting.
.nf

Example
force_sort_criteria=+upnp:class,+upnp:originalTrackNumber,+dc:title

.fi

.IP "\fBwide_links\fP"
Set to 'no' to hide symlinks that point outside user-defined media_dirs.
By default ('yes'), wide symlinks are followed.

.IP "\fBenable_subtitles\fP"
Set to 'no' to disable subtitle support on unknown clients.
By default, subtitles are enabled for unknown or generic clients.



